"阅读下面短文。\nHow AI Is Changing Our Daily Lives\n\nArtificial Intelligence is no longer science fiction. It already shapes everyday life in ways you might not expect.\n\nWhen using apps like TikTok or Douyin, AI algorithms analyze what videos you watch, like, share. Then they recommend content matching your interests. Different people see different feeds on same apps. AI personalizes what you likely enjoy most.\n\nIn education, AI tools help students learn better. Apps correct English pronunciation real-time. Others generate practice math problems suited to your level. AI tutors answer questions 24/7 adapting to each learner's pace. Yet teachers remind us AI cannot replace human creativity in learning.\n\nSmart homes give another example. Smart speakers play music, set alarms, answering questions when spoken to. Smart lights turn off automatically when rooms empty. Some refrigerators even tell you when milk or eggs run low! Such technologies save time making life easier.\n\nOf course challenges exist. Privacy concerns arise because AI collects lots of personal data. Job worries surface too — will robots replace human workers? Experts say AI changes some jobs but also creates new ones. Key is learning skills AI cannot easily match: creative thinking, emotional understanding, teamwork.\n\n(1) How do apps like TikTok choose videos shown?\nA. AI studies your behavior matching tastes\nB. All users see identical video lists\nC. Only popular clips get displayed\nD. Users must pick topics manually daily\n\n(2) What can AI tutoring tools achieve?\nA. Replace human teachers completely now\nB. Answer questions anytime at any pace\nC. Guarantee perfect scores on all exams\nD. Teach social skills better than people\n\n(3) What can smart refrigerators do here?\nA. Order food delivery online automatically\nB. Cook meals whenever you grow busy\nC. Notify you when supplies run quite low\nD. Play music while you enjoy dinner\n\n(4) What concern does the writer mention about AI?\nA. AI devices consume too much electric power\nB. AI equipment costs families too much cash\nC. Privacy risks plus future job market shifts\nD. AI systems break down way too frequently\n\n(5) What skills does AI struggle replacing currently?\nA. Memory calculation plus data processing\nB. Creative thinking plus teamwork ability\nC. Physical strength and quick typing speed\nD. Following instructions repeating tasks",
